       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and there is no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum for inflammatory conditions)\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600 mg/day, which is typical for pain or fever)\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm and give the clinical rationale. I can add it to the order note, though I'd still advise against it."
